# Path to the PCRE installation
PCRE_INCLUDE=/usr/local/include/
PCRE_LIB=/usr/local/lib

# stream-2.8.26's devXxStream.c device support files initialize their DSET
# structs with properly-typed function pointers (e.g. long (*)(dbCommon*))
# against generic DEVSUPFUN (long (*)(void)) struct fields. That was legal
# pre-C23, but C23 redefined empty parens to mean "takes no arguments" (like
# C++), so GCC 15's C23-by-default (Fedora 44, Ubuntu 26.04) now makes this a
# hard type error - same root cause as the busy/seq/sscan/calc fixes.
USR_CFLAGS_Linux += -std=gnu17
